My Lord Cardinal,

You know the disquiet that has long sat upon my conscience touching my marria=
ge to the Queen. The matter can wait no longer.

I charge you to obtain from His Holiness a clean and lawful annulment, and to=
 do so quietly. Spare no effort, and spare me no excuses.

I need not remind you what hangs upon a male heir.

By the King's own hand,
Henry R.
